<p>A drone strike caused a fire on Sunday at an external electrical generator outside the inner perimeter of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant in Abu Dhabi’s Al Dhafra region, UAE authorities said. The Abu Dhabi Media Office and the Federal Authority for Nuclear Regulation said no injuries were reported, radiological safety levels were unaffected and the plant’s essential systems remained ready. The UAE Defence Ministry said three drones entered the country from the direction of the western border, with two “successfully” dealt with and one striking the generator; it said investigations were continuing to determine the source. The UAE Foreign Ministry condemned the incident as an “unprovoked terrorist attack”.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/IzhRw3TLsJw6y8RK1gestiZaEswnhtN4rCbZfMD4eOMSQo92bZs7tS_URZVQCIHvxbYaCMcQVvcuaak_1M0xNFCZSUKUapeANMqef3z-YsUF' alt='A handout picture obtained from the media office of the Barakah Nuclear Power Plant on February 13, 2020, shows a view of the power plant in the western Al Dhafra region of Abu Dhabi.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Backup power: The International Atomic Energy Agency said emergency diesel generators were supplying power to Barakah’s unit 3 and that it was following the situation closely.</li><li>Saudi airspace: Saudi Arabia said it intercepted three drones on the same day after they entered Saudi airspace from Iraq.</li><li>Attribution: No one immediately claimed responsibility, and UAE officials did not publicly blame a specific actor while the source of the strike was under investigation.</li><li>Ceasefire context: Multiple reports said the strike heightened concerns about renewed conflict during a ceasefire between the United States and Iran.</li></ul><blockquote>Military activity that threatens nuclear safety is unacceptable. - Rafael Grossi</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>United Arab Emirates Foreign Ministry: The ministry described the strike as a “dangerous escalation,” an unacceptable act of aggression and a direct threat to the country’s security. (<a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/uae-condemns-drone-strike-caused-fire-outside-nuclear-plant'>The New Arab</a>)</li><li>International Atomic Energy Agency: The IAEA called for “maximum military restraint” near nuclear power plants. (<a href='https://www.brecorder.com/news/40421616/uae-reports-drone-strike-at-nuclear-power-plant'>Business Recorder</a>)</li><li>Iranian Foreign Minister Abbas Araghchi: Araghchi accused the UAE last week of direct involvement in attacks on Iran and said Abu Dhabi did not condemn the initial strikes when they began. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/640111-uae-drone-strike-nuclear-plant/'>RT</a>)</li><li>President Trump: Trump posted after speaking with Netanyahu that Iran must move “FAST,” repeating a warning to Tehran. (<a href='https://www.koreatimes.co.kr/world/20260518/uae-nuclear-plant-targeted-in-drone-strike-amid-iran-tensions'>The Korea Times</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.timesofisrael.com/drone-strike-hits-abu-dhabi-nuclear-plant-uae-saudi-arabia-and-un-watchdog-condemn/'>Drone strike hits Abu Dhabi nuclear plant; UAE, Saudi Arabia and UN watchdog condemn</a> - timesofisrael.com</li><li><a href='https://www.newarab.com/news/uae-condemns-drone-strike-caused-fire-outside-nuclear-plant'>UAE condemns drone strike that caused fire outside nuclear plant</a> - newarab.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/640111-uae-drone-strike-nuclear-plant/'>UAE reports drone strike on nuclear power plant</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/video-drone-targets-uae-nuclear-power-plant-in-latest-blow-to-iran-ceasefire/'>Drone targets UAE nuclear power plant in latest blow to Iran ceasefire</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/us-israel-iran-war-live-updates-lebanon-airstrikes-ceasefire-hezbollah-strait-of-hormuz/article70989557.ece'>Iran-Israel war highlights: Trump